cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RL Lab in your teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "RL Lab: an open-source workbench for training, watching and playing against reinforcement-learning agents"
abstract: >-
  RL Lab is a browser-based dashboard for reinforcement learning. It trains agents across 109
  environments with 9 algorithms (PPO, SAC, TD3, DQN, A2C, QR-DQN, tabular Q-learning, a from-scratch
  neuroevolution and an in-repo AlphaZero), streams the learning process live, lets a human take the
  controls and be graded against their own agent, and aggregates runs across seeds with rliable-style
  statistics (IQM, stratified-bootstrap confidence intervals, performance profiles) exportable to CSV,
  Excel, LaTeX and TensorBoard.
authors:
  - family-names: Svoboda
    given-names: Martin
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Martin8O/RL-Lab"
url: "https://martin8o.github.io/rl-lab-showcase/"
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - deep reinforcement learning
  - education
  - teaching
  - machine learning
  - open source
